PRESERVATION AND DISPLAY CHANGES
original.glb is the untouched Etch binary, renamed locally only. meta.json and
parts.json are unchanged source copies. The model is decoded locally using
Three.js's bundled meshopt decoder; no remote decoder or texture is loaded.
PartExplode centers and uniformly scales the display to a 220 mm overall extent,
bakes static node transforms into actual vertex geometry, recomputes normals,
and groups material regions belonging to the same logical component. Original
mesh shapes, triangle indices and materials are retained. PartExplode adds
component labels, metadata, inspection steps and a reversible exploded view.
Those presentation annotations are not part of the upstream KiCad design.

The source board is 50 x 50 mm with a 1.6 mm thickness, as recorded by Etch.
The 220 mm display extent is not the board's manufactured dimension. The model
has 32 resolved component models plus 8 PCB material layers. The source includes
38 footprints, including holes/artwork and SW1; SW1 has no available source 3D
model and is deliberately omitted rather than replaced by invented geometry.
No electrical netlist, manufacturing verification or physical hardware test is
represented by this visual inspection model.

